1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,593
The trial run for the third arc had one subject: care.

2
00:00:03,593 --> 00:00:14,891
A home-care worker, a night nurse, and a housewife who had raised four children agreed to be interviewed by people who had never done any of those things.

3
00:00:14,891 --> 00:00:19,430
“You want to know what love costs,” the worker said.

4
00:00:19,430 --> 00:00:28,524
“Write it in a file, then come and do a shift.” No one had measured what care cost in the home.

5
00:00:28,524 --> 00:00:41,157
A patient in the ward had a photograph of her husband in a black suit; an old copper coin, a bottle of medicine, and a white envelope sat on the cabinet beside her.

6
00:00:41,157 --> 00:00:46,022
“He was an agent for a textile company,” she said.

7
00:00:46,022 --> 00:00:57,430
“He had a lovely laugh and a lot of debts.” The strike at the plant that winter was the only thing in her file that anyone had bothered to record.

8
00:00:57,430 --> 00:01:05,964
The interview drifted toward inheritance: what a mother passes to a daughter, what a father cannot pass at all.

9
00:01:05,964 --> 00:01:09,998
“A child is not stock,” she said.

10
00:01:09,998 --> 00:01:22,732
“And a marriage is not an alliance.” Her own intimacy with her husband had survived exile from the south, an empty counter, and a queue for everything.

11
00:01:22,732 --> 00:01:32,210
Her companion in the next bed was a former teacher; his buddy came every Thursday with a lamb stew and a paper tag on the container.

12
00:01:32,210 --> 00:01:35,975
“A friend is not a limb,” she said.

13
00:01:35,975 --> 00:01:51,387
“You cannot cut one off and call the rest whole.” The terror of the empty chair was familiar to everyone in the ward, and the hostility of the young nurse toward tears was, in its own way, an affection.

14
00:01:51,387 --> 00:01:55,557
She held his arm like a professional.

15
00:01:55,557 --> 00:02:04,166
A woman from the city cabinet arrived to represent the council, wearing a suit and carrying a lens in a leather case.

16
00:02:04,166 --> 00:02:07,880
“Tell me what you found,” she said.

17
00:02:07,880 --> 00:02:21,359
“That is what we know: one pulse, one queen, one snake in the grass.” Her pulse was steady; her tail, as she left, was a cold goodbye.

18
00:02:21,359 --> 00:02:38,671
“Since you asked,” Maya said, “we found that people care whether the person writing the file can imagine their life.” A line of chairs, a single emotion on every face: this was the evidence nobody had asked for.

19
00:02:38,671 --> 00:02:51,734
One ally in the cabinet was often enough; when the new file reached the other desk, a person who had never met them would read it, and that was more than what the old system could claim.

20
00:02:51,734 --> 00:02:56,671
Whether the council would act was another matter.
